VA-API (va plugin and libgstva) on illumos: use the DRM display and the
/dev/dri/renderD* scan, as on Linux.  illumos has libva-drm and DRM render
nodes; without gudev the plugin probes renderD128.. directly.

Not yet upstream (OpenIndiana local patch).

--- gst-plugins-bad-1.28.9/gst-libs/gst/va/meson.build.orig
+++ gst-plugins-bad-1.28.9/gst-libs/gst/va/meson.build
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@
               '-DBUILDING_GST_VA',
               '-DG_LOG_DOMAIN="GStreamer-VA"']
 
-if host_system not in ['linux', 'windows']
+if host_system not in ['linux', 'sunos', 'windows']
   subdir_done()
 endif
 
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@
   subdir_done()
 endif
 
-if host_system == 'linux'
+if host_system in ['linux', 'sunos']
   libva_drm_dep = dependency('libva-drm', version: libva_req, required: va_required)
   if not libva_drm_dep.found()
     subdir_done()
--- gst-plugins-bad-1.28.9/sys/va/meson.build.orig
+++ gst-plugins-bad-1.28.9/sys/va/meson.build
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@
   'va': pathsep.join(doc_sources)
 }
 
-if host_system not in ['linux', 'windows']
+if host_system not in ['linux', 'sunos', 'windows']
   subdir_done()
 endif
 
@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@
 extra_dep = []
 c_std_arg = ['c_std=c99']
 
-if host_system == 'linux'
+if host_system in ['linux', 'sunos']
   libgudev_dep = dependency('gudev-1.0', required: get_option('udev'), allow_fallback: true)
   if libgudev_dep.found()
     extra_args += ['-DHAVE_GUDEV']
